    <desc>Where CA-1 meets US-101 at the coast, under the railway trestle. Hike-and-bike campsites confirmed; drinking water, restrooms/showers, camp store. Open August 2026, reservable via ReserveCalifornia. (805) 968-1033. Stops day 2 at 285 km instead of 303 km, at the cost of a longer day 3. Known to be windy. SRC parks.ca.gov Gaviota page  [day2_limekiln_refugio km 285, 338 m off route]</desc>
